.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-TTY1 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-tty1
.Nd start the first console: the install menu on the live medium when asked for, a login everywhere else
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar tty
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The drop-in for
.Pa getty@tty1.service
runs
.Nm
in place of
.Xr agetty 8 .
On the live medium booted with
.Ql kldload.tui=1
on the kernel command line it logs root in with no password, and root's
login profile starts
.Ql kld install ;
in every other case it is the ordinary login prompt.
The same drop-in reaches installed systems, so it decides when the
console opens rather than through the unit's conditions, and the worst it
can do is a normal login.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
For tests only:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KLDLOAD_TTY1_CMDLINE
A file to read instead of
.Pa /proc/cmdline .
.It Ev KLDLOAD_TTY1_LIVE
Directories to look for instead of the live mounts.
.It Ev KLDLOAD_TTY1_DRYRUN
1 prints the
.Xr agetty 8
command instead of running it.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
It becomes
.Xr agetty 8 ;
with
.Ev KLDLOAD_TTY1_DRYRUN ,
0.
.Sh EXAMPLES
What it would run, with its test settings, on 2026-09-30: a live medium
with
.Ql kldload.tui=1 ,
a live medium without it, and an installed system:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
/sbin/agetty --autologin root --noclear tty1 linux
/sbin/agetty --noclear tty1 linux
/sbin/agetty --noclear tty1 linux
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr agetty 8 ,
.Xr kld 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-13 a separate unit that fought the login for tty1 cost the
kiosk two days; this replaced that approach.
